From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:24:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] 
 alloc_tag-introduce-ioctls-to-toggle-allocation-tracepoints-fix-fix

mark alloc_tag_is_traced __always_inline also, per Hao Ge

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Abhishek Bapat <abhishekbapat@google.com>
Cc: Hao Ge <hao.ge@linux.dev>
Cc: Suren Baghdasaryan <surenb@google.com>
---
 include/linux/alloc_tag.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/alloc_tag.h b/include/linux/alloc_tag.h
index 00eca9bf81903..3516137649ccf 100644
--- a/include/linux/alloc_tag.h
+++ b/include/linux/alloc_tag.h
@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@ static inline void alloc_tag_clear_traced(struct alloc_tag *tag)
 	atomic_andnot(CODETAG_FLAG_TRACE_ON, &tag->ct.flags);
 }
 
-static inline bool alloc_tag_is_traced(const struct alloc_tag *tag)
+static __always_inline inline bool alloc_tag_is_traced(const struct alloc_tag *tag)
 {
 	return !!(atomic_read(&tag->ct.flags) & CODETAG_FLAG_TRACE_ON);
 }
-- 
2.47.3

